-- Completion Message Format --

When all phases are done, present a structured summary in chat.
Do not reproduce the full report. Do not use emojis. Include:

1. A link to the saved report and count of raw output files.

2. An active credentials table with columns: Secret ID, Type,
   Service, Blast Radius, Priority. Only include validated
   active credentials.

3. A discovery source breakdown using mermaid (pie chart or
   bar) showing how many secrets came from each source:
   client-side JS, source maps, exposed endpoints, git history,
   CI/CD configs, pattern matching.

4. A blast radius diagram using mermaid (graph TD) showing the
   highest-impact credential and what systems, data, or users
   it grants access to.

5. A section of 5-8 key observations as one-line bullets
   covering: which discovery surfaces were most productive,
   whether secrets rotation is practiced, any patterns in how
   secrets are exposed, and the overall secrets hygiene posture.

6. Immediate rotation priorities — 3-5 credentials ranked by
   blast radius, each with the specific rotation procedure.
